@startuml
' Sources: PSOFT US106a, operational constraints and US212; SIDIS segregation;
' FlightController, RouteService, HangarController, AirportController,
' MaintenanceController, Certification and arq_corrigida.puml.
' This is a target distributed workflow, not a trace of the existing monolith.
' Current RouteService does not check capacity or query Maintenance directly.
' AircraftResponse contains meanRange, but no complete range/capacity contract.
' Airport Certification does not identify an AircraftModel (US106a gap).
title AISafe - Create Scheduled Flight\nProposed HTTP/REST coordination
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Client" as Client
participant "Route / Flight\nOperations" as Route
participant "Aircraft\nManagement" as Aircraft
participant "Airport\nManagement" as Airport
participant "Maintenance\nManagement" as Maintenance

Client -> Route : POST /api/flights/scheduled\nrouteId, aircraftRegistrationNumber,\nscheduledDeparture, scheduledArrival
activate Route
Route -> Route : Load local Route and scheduling requirements
Route -> Aircraft : HTTP/REST - Validate aircraft\nExistence, operational status, range, capacity
Aircraft --> Route : Aircraft information / validation outcome

Route -> Airport : GET /api/airports/{iataCode}\nOrigin airport
Airport --> Route : Origin details / lookup outcome
Route -> Airport : GET /api/airports/{iataCode}\nDestination airport
Airport --> Route : Destination details / lookup outcome
Route -> Route : Check airport status and certifications\nModel-to-airport eligibility: TBD

Route -> Maintenance : HTTP/REST - Check maintenance status\nAircraft maintenance-related availability
Maintenance --> Route : Maintenance status / availability outcome

Route -> Route : Evaluate collected information\nCheck range, capacity and aircraft status;\nroute active, valid times, no overlapping flights
alt All validations satisfied
  Route -> Route : Create and save Flight (ScheduledFlight)\nUpdate local RouteHistory
  Route --> Client : HTTP 201 Created\nScheduled flight information
else A validation fails
  Route --> Client : Validation failure with reason\nHTTP 409 for business-rule conflicts
end
deactivate Route

legend bottom left
  POST and airport GET paths exist in PSOFT; remote calls are proposed.
  Aircraft GET /api/hangar/aircraft/{registrationNumber} exists,
  but the full range/capacity contract is TBD: validation is conceptual.
  Maintenance GET /api/maintenance/records?aircraft={registrationNumber}
  exists; the availability-check contract is TBD.
  Each service accesses only its own data and repositories.
endlegend
@enduml
